<div class="arn-art">
  <p>Use the token art and portraits from art modules you have installed (a token pack, a bestiary or adventure module with creature art), or folders of images in your Data, matched to the Bestiary's monsters by name. Nothing is copied: tokens point at the images where they are, so keep the module installed (it can stay switched off) and the folders where they are. Art you set by hand is never replaced.</p>

  <h3>1. Art modules to use</h3>
  <p class="hint">Ticked to start with: the ones that look like art packs. Scan uses the ticks as they are.</p>
  <div class="arn-art-mods">
    {{#each mods}}
    <label class="arn-art-mod"><input type="checkbox" name="mod" value="{{id}}" {{#if checked}}checked{{/if}}> {{title}} <span class="arn-muted">{{id}}</span></label>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  <h3>1b. Folders in your Data (optional)</h3>
  <p class="hint">A token pack you downloaded as plain images rather than a module: unzip it into your Foundry Data folder (for example <code>art/dnd-tokens</code>) and add it here, one folder per line.</p>
  <textarea name="folders" rows="3" placeholder="art/dnd-tokens">{{folders}}</textarea>
  <p><button type="button" data-action="pickFolder"><i class="fa-solid fa-folder-open"></i> Pick a folder</button></p>

  <div class="arn-art-order-box {{#unless order.length}}hidden{{/unless}}">
    <h3>1c. Which art comes first</h3>
    <p class="hint">When more than one has art for a monster, the higher one's is used, even if a lower one's name fits more closely. Use the arrows, then Scan.</p>
    <ol class="arn-art-order">
      {{#each order}}
      <li data-source="{{key}}"><span class="arn-art-order-name">{{label}}</span>{{#if count}}<span class="arn-muted">{{countText}}</span>{{/if}}<span class="arn-art-order-move"><button type="button" data-action="moveUp" data-tooltip="Higher: its art wins"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up"></i></button><button type="button" data-action="moveDown" data-tooltip="Lower"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down"></i></button></span></li>
      {{/each}}
    </ol>
  </div>

  <p>
    <button type="button" data-action="scan"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i> Scan</button>
    {{#if names}}<span class="arn-muted">Art for {{names}} Bestiary monsters{{#if near}} ({{near}} by a close name or folder, such as "goblin" in goblin_warrior.webp){{/if}}; {{images}} images looked at{{#if scanned}}, scanned {{scanned}}{{/if}}.</span>{{else}}<span class="arn-muted">Not scanned yet.</span>{{/if}}
    <span class="arn-art-changed hidden arn-bad">Changed: press Scan to use the new list.</span>
  </p>

  {{#if missing.length}}
  <details class="arn-art-missing"><summary>{{missing.length}} Bestiary monsters without art</summary>
    <p class="hint">No image named after them in the packs and folders above. These keep the Arneyan icon.</p>
    <p class="arn-art-missing-list">{{#each missing}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}</p>
  </details>
  {{/if}}

  <h3>2. Use it</h3>
  <label class="arn-art-mod"><input type="checkbox" name="auto" {{#if auto}}checked{{/if}}> New monsters from the Bestiary get matched art (saved as soon as you tick it)</label>
  <p>
    <button type="button" data-action="apply" {{#unless names}}disabled{{/unless}}><i class="fa-solid fa-wand-magic-sparkles"></i> Use on monsters already here</button>
    <span class="arn-muted">Bestiary monsters, and their tokens, still showing an Arneyan icon.</span>
  </p>
</div>
